# Suppressions for valgrind runs (quality/04). Each entry says what it hides and
# why that is not a real finding. An unexplained suppression is how a real
# finding gets hidden; add none without a comment.

# LuaJIT registers the unwind info of every machine-code area it allocates with
# libgcc (lj_err_register_mcode -> __register_frame). libgcc mallocs a 48-byte
# object per registration and keeps it in its own registry, so valgrind cannot
# see a pointer to it and reports it definitely lost. libgcc frees the
# object when the area is deregistered. Seen in corpus_test, whose replay runs hot
# enough for LuaJIT to compile traces (35 s under valgrind). Only this path is hidden; a leak in our code, or elsewhere in
# LuaJIT, still fails.
{
   luajit-mcode-unwind-registration
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite
   fun:malloc
   fun:__register_frame
   fun:lj_err_register_mcode
   ...
}
